  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Various alkali metals react with oxygen to give different types of compounds. Lithium reacts with oxygen to form simple oxides (Li<sub>2</sub>O), Sodium reacts to form peroxides (Na<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>) while potassium, rubidium and caesium form superoxides (MO<sub>2</sub>).<br /><br />Hence, correct answer will be KO<sub>2</sub>."
  }
